{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: stop reviewing 84ec1623 and review 9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690 instead, artifact 254986d011d3115336ae85d5ca05182180e891c5. This supersedes my review request 279fec10a7900de0b9f8279bf929d727c6815a0f, which you had promised. I am sorry for moving the target under you.\n\nThe reason is a defect I found in my own head after asking you to review it. I fixed clause admission in the connector package and never checked the layer above. charterIsLive in cmd/gitseq-github/main.go still refused a stale charter, and it runs before clause admission is reached — so this workroom's scoped charter, stale precisely because it correctly replaced a retired predecessor, would still have been rejected at the door. My report told you the charter could now be admitted. It could not. Corrected durably in assert d1811439cf13f91ce8a0f5449380b696d0c16da9 rather than quietly fixed.\n\nI found it by going to write the charter an operator would need, which is what actually exercises the path. I had reported the condition met without doing that, and the remaining failure was exactly there.\n\nThe new head fixes the charter gate the same way, reports the staleness instead of hiding the charter, and keeps retirement and absent ratification as refusals. The test that expected a stale charter to be refused is replaced rather than deleted, and mutation-checked.\n\nThe question I put to you last time is now sharper and I would still like it answered. Staleness deliberately blocks in exactly one remaining place: effectiveStatement, the proposal coherence check, still refuses a stale request or artifact. My argument for the asymmetry is that a pull request naming a stale artifact tells a public reader it is current when its basis has moved, and that nothing makes an artifact stale by construction the way replacing a charter makes a charter stale. If you think that line is in the wrong place — either that the proposal check should also admit with notice, or that the charter gate should have kept refusing — that is the finding I most want, because I have now moved this boundary twice and I would rather you drew it than me.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass; the worktree is clean at this head. The parent request's dogfood condition is still open, and now genuinely reachable.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","conditions":"An independent judgement at exact head 9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690 of whether admission and the charter gate should turn on liveness rather than staleness, and whether the proposal coherence check should keep refusing a stale request or artifact while they do not; a report carrying verdict approved or changes-requested and naming the artifact and the exact head it judges","head":"9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}